body: "pm-changelog 2026.11.7 uses `const DEPENDABOT_SUBJECT = /^[\\w-]+\\((?:deps|deps-dev)\\): bump /` in generator.ts. The lowercase-only `bump` rejects actual squash subjects such as `Build(deps-dev): Bump the pm-toolchain group across 1 directory with 3 updates (#106)`.\n\nReproduction: create a full Git repository with an older release tag and CHANGELOG section, only older closed items without release fields, then commit the subject above and request a newer release using `--since-previous-tag --until-release-tag --release-version-from-package --respect-item-release`. It raises MISSING_REQUESTED_RELEASE instead of emitting the dependency-only section. Lowercasing only `Bump` makes it succeed.\n\nPublic failing evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/actions/runs/43009061713 (job 130483756140). All 41 unassigned items are before the prior tag; this is not evidence that they need reassignment. Four new dependency bumps are ignored. In contrast https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/actions/runs/43059359608 succeeded today using the same flags and lowercase `bump` subjects, producing real dependency notes.\n\nPlease recognize the capitalization used by Dependabot/squash titles while retaining the deps/deps-dev scope and bump verb requirement. Add single-window and all-release-tags tests for capitalized Bump, including regeneration after tagging, and keep unrelated deps fixes excluded. pm-jev will use an in-repo preparation workaround without changing this package or its pin.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-11T23:30:52Z)\n>\n> Update: we are fixing this here in pm-changelog rather than with the in-repo workaround mentioned above. unbraind/pm-jev#110 is closed. A PR on branch `fix/dependency-bump-subject-case` will follow, with one shared, case-insensitive verb matcher (scope `deps`/`deps-dev` and the `bump` verb still required) and must-allow and must-refuse tests. pm-jev and pm-swarm both use the capitalized subject style."
